Being at the center of Shibuya and all, there were plenty of 3D DQN women and office drones occupying it, but since the rooms were all%Nprivate, that wasn’t an issue.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005660)
As for the room I was in, it was the one I always reserved: Room 37, located way in the back.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005670)
It was pretty inconvenient to get refills, but since very few%Npeople ever reserved rooms near the back, it was nice and quiet.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005680)
Once or twice a week, I’d come here on my way home from school to%Nlog on to my other ESO account.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005690)
Neidhardt was essentially a celebrity, so this was my way to just%Nrelax and enjoy the game.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000056A0)
While I did love being treated like a hero all the time, it sure did take its toll.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005718)
That was why I’d made another 
<DICT>
avatar
</DICT>
.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005730)
This one was a female character named “Liselotte.”
<LINE>
I hadn’t accomplished anything big with her—I’d mainly just made%Nher to help Neidhardt look even better by comparison.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005758)
I played for about three hours to blow off some steam. I then had%Nsome fun messing around with my 
<DICT>
guild
</DICT>
 mates while talking about%Nhardcore 
<DICT>
doujins
</DICT>
 and other random shit.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005836)
By the time I’d left the café, it was already around 9 PM.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005846)
There were even more DQNs around at this time of night.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005856)
They’d line the streets like they owned the place, stuffing their%Nfaces with greasy-ass hamburgers as they let out the most%Ndisgusting laughter imaginable. Just looking at them made me want%Nto puke.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005866)
And what was especially bad? If you just so much as looked at them%Nthe wrong way, they’d immediately come and beat the shit out of you. Fucking savages.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005876)
They weren’t human—they were animals.%NNot fit for civilized society.
<LINE>
Just throw them in a slaughterhouse or something. Seriously.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005886)
Well, I say that, but there was no way I could hope to ever stand up to them myself. So there was no point in trying.%NRegardless, it was time to get the hell out of Center-
<DICT>
gai
</DICT>
.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005932)
On my way back from @café, I always dropped by Mangadarake, which%Nwas pretty close by, or Animeight, which was a bit further off.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005942)
I decided to check out Animeight today, so I headed toward the%Nstation’s south exit.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005952)
Down that path, there was an instant drop in the number of DQNs.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005962)
Man, Center-gai was complete and utter chaos... Just walking%Nthrough it brought me nothing but pain and suffering. I’d never%Nset foot there again if I could help it.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005972)
I wish the whole place would just get blown to smithereens—except%N@café and Mangadarake, of course.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005982)
All right then, time to go browsing for some comics, doujins, or%Nwhatever else catches my eye.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005992)
Oh yeah, that’s right—the Blood Tune Vol. 5 DVD was coming out soon. Was it available for pre-order yet? If so, I definitely needed to%Nget one nailed down.
<END>
